CCTPBridgeModule_Execute
├── when params length is less than minimum encoding size
│   └── it should return failed result with "Invalid params encoding"
├── when params are empty
│   └── it should return failed result with "Invalid params encoding"
├── when amount is zero
│   └── it should return failed result with "Zero bridge amount"
├── when token is not USDC
│   └── it should return failed result with "Only USDC supported"
├── when mint recipient is zero
│   └── it should return failed result with "Zero mint recipient"
├── when finality threshold is invalid
│   └── it should return failed result with "Invalid finality threshold"
├── when maxFeeBps equals 10000
│   └── it should return failed result with "Invalid max fee bps"
├── when maxFeeBps exceeds 10000
│   └── it should return failed result with "Invalid max fee bps"
├── when caller has insufficient balance
│   └── it should return failed result with "Insufficient balance"
├── when token transfer from caller fails
│   └── it should return failed result with "Token transfer failed"
├── when no-return token (e.g. USDT)
│   └── it should succeed and bridge despite missing return value
├── given params without hook data
│   ├── when tokenMessenger reverts
│   │   └── it should revert (propagate CCTP revert)
│   └── when depositForBurn succeeds
│       ├── it should call depositForBurn on tokenMessenger
│       ├── it should pass correct arguments to tokenMessenger
│       ├── it should revoke tokenMessenger approval after burn
│       ├── it should emit BridgeInitiated
│       ├── it should return success result with (amount - computedMaxFee) as amountOut
│       ├── it should return encoded domain and recipient in data field
│       └── it should transfer USDC from caller to module
├── given params with hook data
│   └── when depositForBurnWithHook succeeds
│       ├── it should call depositForBurnWithHook on tokenMessenger
│       ├── it should pass hookData to tokenMessenger
│       ├── it should emit BridgeInitiated with hookData
│       └── it should return success result
├── given params with standard finality
│   └── when bridge succeeds
│       └── it should pass minFinalityThreshold 2000 to tokenMessenger
├── when called by any address
│   └── it should succeed (execute is permissionless)
├── when amount is 1 and computed maxFee rounds to zero
│   └── it should succeed with full amount as amountOut
├── when destination caller is set
│   └── it should pass destinationCaller to tokenMessenger
├── when executed consecutively
│   └── it should succeed on both calls
├── when bridging to different domains
│   └── it should route each bridge to its own domain
└── fuzz
    ├── it should succeed for any valid amount [fuzz]
    └── it should return full amount when maxFeeBps is zero [fuzz]
